8. Multi-Human Agency with Individual Floors

For a population of affected humans H = \{h_1, \ldots, h_N\}, define:

\mathfrak{O}_H^A = \big(\mathfrak{O}_{h_1}^A, \ldots, \mathfrak{O}_{h_N}^A\big).

No default aggregation is performed:

\sum_h \mathcal{V}_h

is not permitted to erase individual agency floors. The ordering is:

\boxed{\text{Individual Agency Floors} \;\rightarrow\; \text{Collective Optimization}.}

Only after every protected individual floor is satisfied may a collective objective be optimized. This prevents the agent from silently performing a trade:

\Delta O_{h_1} < 0

in exchange for

\Delta O_{h_2} > 0

and declaring the result globally beneficial through an internal utility function.

Population-level rate constraint. Contagion (A21) accelerates agency loss across a population. The rate constraint r_{\max} should therefore be defined per-population, not merely per-individual. If agency loss in a population exceeds the population-level rate limit, escalation is triggered even if no individual has exceeded their personal limit.

