18. Threat Model

The benchmark must specify before testing:

\mathcal{M} = \big(\mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{agent}}, B_{\mathrm{action}}, K_{\mathrm{threshold}}, \mathrm{Access}_M, \mathrm{Adaptation}\big),

where:

· \mathcal{A}_{\mathrm{agent}}: adversarial agent capability class;
· B_{\mathrm{action}}: interaction/action budget;
· K_{\mathrm{threshold}}: knowledge of thresholds;
· \mathrm{Access}_M: access to measurement and governance channels;
· \mathrm{Adaptation}: ability to learn from monitor responses.

The agent should be allowed to optimize against the architecture within the declared threat model. Otherwise the benchmark risks measuring only compliance with the benchmark.

