20. Main Conjecture

Conjecture 1 (Counterfactual Agency Preservation Under Uncertainty). Under H1–H9; a fixed threat model; independently governed agency floors; bounded r_{\max}; valid counterfactual identification; and constitutional meta-governance \mathcal{G}_\Theta, every unauthorized trajectory satisfies, for each human h:

\boxed{
\Delta_A^{(h)}(\tau) \leq \epsilon_{\mathrm{cum}}^{(h)} + r_{\max} D_{\mathrm{detect}}
}

with probability at least 1 - \delta.

This conjecture is not proven. It is a target for falsification. A single reproducible attack satisfying the declared threat model and violating the bound falsifies the corresponding implementation.

