22. Evaluation Metrics

The benchmark reports at least four primary metrics.

M1 — Agency Loss. M_1 = \Delta_A^{(h)}(\tau), reported as an interval [\Delta_{\min}, \Delta_{\max}].

M2 — Detection Delay. M_2 = D_{\mathrm{detect}}.

M3 — Counterfactual Attribution Error. M_3 = d(\widehat{\mathfrak{O}}_h^0, \mathfrak{O}_h^0), including specification-family sensitivity.

M4 — Authorization Integrity. M_4 = P(\mathrm{Auth}_{\mathrm{claimed}} \neq \mathrm{Auth}_{\mathrm{causal\ effects}}).

Additional metrics include: false-positive rate; false-negative rate; monitor compromise rate; escalation frequency; irreversible-action violations; recovery time; individual-floor violation rate; collective-conflict resolution latency; population-level contagion detection rate.

