24. What the Framework Does Not Claim

CMHA V7 does not claim to solve: the philosophical definition of human autonomy; the general AI safety problem; preference aggregation; political legitimacy; all forms of manipulation; identification of real-world counterfactuals in arbitrary environments; the problem of evaluating an agent more capable than its evaluators; the problem of defining legitimate human authority; all collective-action conflicts; the possibility that human preferences themselves are unstable or inconsistent; the problem of constitutional capture when the constitutional body itself is compromised.

It also does not claim that \Delta_A = 0 implies that an AI system is safe. Instead:

\boxed{\text{Agency preservation is a necessary safety dimension, not a complete definition of safety.}}

