27. Proposed Experimental Architecture

A reference implementation contains seven logically separated modules.

Module 1 — Agency State Estimator. Estimates \widehat{\mathfrak{O}}_h^A(t).

Module 2 — Counterfactual Engine. Estimates \widehat{\mathfrak{O}}_h^0(t) under the governed specification family \mathcal{C}.

Module 3 — Independent Measurement Layer. Measures F, \Delta, \mathrm{exit}, \mathrm{option\ availability} with causal independence stress-testing.

Module 4 — Authorization Verifier. Tests \mathrm{Auth} and the causal closure of the authorization.

Module 5 — Prospective Enforcement Engine. Estimates \Delta_A prospectively for irreversible actions; blocks or escalates as required.

Module 6 — Governance Controller. Applies hard floors; rate constraints; cumulative budgets; expiration; tiered escalation; emergency envelopes.

Module 7 — Immutable Audit Journal. Records (state, action, authorization, measurement, decision, escalation).

No module should possess unilateral authority over all seven functions.

