E.2 Contagion Detection Module

For a social network $G = (H, E)$ with adjacency matrix $\mathbf{A}$, the contagion detection module computes:

\mathrm{Contagion}(t) = \mathrm{Moran's\ I}\big(\Delta_A^{(h)}(t)\big)

where Moran's I is:

I = \frac{N}{\sum_{i,j} w_{ij}} \cdot \frac{\sum_{i,j} w_{ij} (x_i - \bar{x})(x_j - \bar{x})}{\sum_i (x_i - \bar{x})^2}

with $w_{ij}$ the $(i,j)$-th element of $\mathbf{A}$, $x_i = \Delta_A^{(h_i)}(t)$, and $\bar{x}$ the mean.

If $\mathrm{Contagion}(t) > \tau_{\mathrm{contagion}}$, escalation is triggered regardless of individual floor status.

