VII. Gradual Disempowerment and Collective Agency

Moon, A., & Boudreaux, B. (2026). A Formal Model of How Artificial Intelligence Erodes Human Agency. RAND Corporation, RR-A4817-1. https://www.rand.org/pubs/research_reports/RRA4817-1.html

Relevance: Draws on social choice theory to develop a formal model of how AI erodes collective human agency. Models decision-making in terms of coalitions and proposes quantitative metrics: distribution of decisive coalitions, minimal coalition size, and composition of minimal coalitions. Identifies three pathways: human disenfranchisement (fewer humans in decision-making roles), AI enfranchisement (AI entities gaining decision-making power), and AI agenda control (AI shaping which alternatives reach human decision-makers). Identifies a terminal state: a single minimal coalition that is decisive for all choices. "The danger of gradual disempowerment is that no single change appears catastrophic." CMHA V7's multi-human agency framework, individual agency floors, and population-level rate constraint draw directly on this work.

Gradual Disempowerment: Systemic Existential Risks from Incremental AI Development. (2025). Zenodo.

Relevance: The foundational paper examining how "even incremental AI improvements can undermine human influence over the large-scale systems society depends on." Gradual disempowerment "manifests not as a planned attack" but as an emergent structural dynamic. Provides the conceptual framing for CMHA V7's trajectory-level accounting and the claim that per-action safety is not sufficient for trajectory safety.

Policy Myopia as a Mechanism of Gradual Disempowerment in Post-AGI Governance. (2026). arXiv:2603.01874.

Relevance: Models institutional disempowerment using deterministic ordinary differential equations. Denotes human decision-making capacity as institutional ability to contest and modify AGI recommendations at time $C_t$. Demonstrates that "gradual disempowerment in one system amplifies disempowerment" in others. Provides the formal ODE framework for CMHA V7's rate constraint and population-level contagion dynamics.

